The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail because it returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to crash with an IndexError because there was no second element

I've fixed it by changing the index from 1 to 0, and both tests now pass successfully.
